  nesnd_supply_rules:0 "#bold Latest refresh#!\nUnemployed workforce: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_supply_unemployed').GetValue|0] / [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_supply_workforce').GetValue|0]#! (#v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_supply_unemployment').GetValue|%1]#!)\nStates beyond the local unemployment limit: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_supply_critical_states').GetValue|0]#!\n\n#bold Employment requirements#!\nUnemployed workers may be at most #v 12%#! of the national workforce. In states with at least #v 50,000#! workers, the limit is #v 20%#!. Subsistence workers count as employed. Statistics refresh weekly and when arrangements change; completion checks current conditions.\n\nEach required school, barracks, workshop or administrative facility must have at least one building staffed to #v 75%#! without input shortages. Check its hiring tooltip for [concept_pop_qualifications], [concept_building_wage] and [concept_good]. Education, suitable vacancies and market supplies can support occupational transitions. There must be no famine, no local grain shortage and no more than a #v 25%#! grain price increase.\n\nContinue in the shared market, approach a foreign partner, or arrange purchases domestically. All four requirements must hold for #v 12 consecutive weeks#!; war, market changes or failed requirements restart the count."
